  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sudharshana vs The Designated Officer on 2 July, 2018 Author: M.Govindaraj Bench: M.Govindaraj Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 02.07.2018 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Govindaraj W.P.(Md) No.13798 of 2018 and W.M.P.(MD).No.12513 of 2018 1.Sudharshana 2.A.Varshika ... Petitioners vs. 1.The Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, (Food Safety Wing) Thanjavur. 2.V.Geetha ... Respondents",
    "facts": "The writ petition has been filed for issuance of writ of Mandamus, forbearing the first respondent for renewing or issuing any license under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 to the second respondent or any other person claiming under her in the petitioners' premises No.7, Ess-Vee Towers Ground Floor, Nageswaran South Street, Kumbakonam, Thanjavur District. Sudharshana vs The Designated Officer on 2 July, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/118590719/ 1 2.The petitioners are the owners of the premises No.7, Ess-Vee Towers Ground Floor, Nageswaran South Street, Kumbakonam, Thanjavur District. They let out the same to one Elumalai for doing business. Thereafter, the said tenant Elumalai had handed over the property to the second respondent. It appears that out of some money transaction, the property was sublet to the second respondent. During the earlier round of litigation, supply of electricity was questioned before this Court and it was decided in favour of the petitioners. Thereafter, the second respondent applied for licence for conducting the hotel business. 3.The learned counsel appearing for the petitioners would contend that the petitioners submitted their objections to the first respondent not to renew the licence, as per the statutory provisions under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The first respondent has acknowledged the receipt of representations and are pending before the first respondent. Therefore, the petitioners are before this Court with a limited prayer of seeking direction directing the first respondent to consider their objections, before renewing the licence in favour of the second respondent.",
